{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Chapter 2: Potential Outcomes Framework\n",
    "## Implementation & Demonstration Notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements key concepts from *A First Course in Causal Inference*, Chapter 2:\n",
    "- Science Table construction\n",
    "- SUTVA verification\n",
    "- Treatment assignment mechanism comparison (Perfect Doctor vs. Clueless Doctor)\n",
    "- Subgroup causal effects & Yule-Simpson impossibility\n",
    "- Nonlinear estimands (median treatment effects)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from scipy import stats\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Constructing the Science Table"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "n = 500\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate potential outcomes\n",
    "Y0 = np.random.normal(0, 1, n)          # Control potential outcomes\n",
    "tau = -0.5 + Y0                          # Individual causal effects (heterogeneous)\n",
    "Y1 = Y0 + tau                            # Treatment potential outcomes\n",
    "\n",
    "# Build the Science Table (normally invisible — shown here for illustration)\n",
    "science_table = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'i': range(1, n+1),\n",
    "    'Yi(1)': Y1,\n",
    "    'Yi(0)': Y0,\n",
    "    'tau_i': tau\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "true_ace = science_table['tau_i'].mean()\n",
    "print(f'True Average Causal Effect (ACE): {true_ace:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'Std of individual effects: {tau.std():.4f}')\n",
    "science_table.head(10)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Treatment Assignment: Perfect Doctor vs. Clueless Doctor\n",
    "\n",
    "Demonstrating how the treatment assignment mechanism drastically affects\n",
    "the naive difference-in-means estimator."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --- Perfect Doctor: treats if tau >= 0 ---\n",
    "Z_perfect = (tau >= 0).astype(int)\n",
    "Y_obs_perfect = Z_perfect * Y1 + (1 - Z_perfect) * Y0\n",
    "did_perfect = Y_obs_perfect[Z_perfect == 1].mean() - Y_obs_perfect[Z_perfect == 0].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Clueless Doctor: random assignment (coin flip) ---\n",
    "Z_random = np.random.binomial(1, 0.5, n)\n",
    "Y_obs_random = Z_random * Y1 + (1 - Z_random) * Y0\n",
    "did_random = Y_obs_random[Z_random == 1].mean() - Y_obs_random[Z_random == 0].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=' * 55)\n",
    "print(f'{\"True ACE\":<30s}: {true_ace:+.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'{\"Perfect Doctor (DiM)\":<30s}: {did_perfect:+.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'{\"Clueless Doctor (DiM)\":<30s}: {did_random:+.4f}')\n",
    "print('=' * 55)\n",
    "print('\\nThe Perfect Doctor reverses the sign of the estimated effect!')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Visualization: Observed Outcomes Under Each Mechanism"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(16, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# True distribution of individual effects\n",
    "axes[0].hist(tau, bins=30, color='#6d4aff', alpha=0.7, edgecolor='white')\n",
    "axes[0].axvline(true_ace, color='red', linewidth=2, linestyle='--', label=f'True ACE = {true_ace:.2f}')\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Distribution of Individual Causal Effects', fontsize=12)\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel(r'$\\tau_i$'); axes[0].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Perfect Doctor\n",
    "axes[1].bar(['Treated', 'Control'], \n",
    "            [Y_obs_perfect[Z_perfect==1].mean(), Y_obs_perfect[Z_perfect==0].mean()],\n",
    "            color=['#6d4aff', '#c4b8ff'], edgecolor='white')\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(f'Perfect Doctor\\nDiM = {did_perfect:.2f} (True: {true_ace:.2f})', fontsize=12)\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel('Mean Observed Outcome')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Clueless Doctor\n",
    "axes[2].bar(['Treated', 'Control'],\n",
    "            [Y_obs_random[Z_random==1].mean(), Y_obs_random[Z_random==0].mean()],\n",
    "            color=['#6d4aff', '#c4b8ff'], edgecolor='white')\n",
    "axes[2].set_title(f'Clueless Doctor (RCT)\\nDiM = {did_random:.2f} (True: {true_ace:.2f})', fontsize=12)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Subgroup Analysis & Yule-Simpson Impossibility\n",
    "\n",
    "If both subgroup causal effects are positive, the overall ACE must be positive.\n",
    "We verify this numerically."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a binary subgroup variable X\n",
    "X = np.random.binomial(1, 0.5, n)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute subgroup causal effects\n",
    "mask1 = (X == 1)\n",
    "mask0 = (X == 0)\n",
    "\n",
    "tau1 = tau[mask1].mean()  # Subgroup 1 ACE\n",
    "tau0 = tau[mask0].mean()  # Subgroup 0 ACE\n",
    "pi1 = mask1.mean()         # Proportion in subgroup 1\n",
    "pi0 = mask0.mean()         # Proportion in subgroup 0\n",
    "\n",
    "ace_check = pi1 * tau1 + pi0 * tau0\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Subgroup 1: τ₁ = {tau1:.4f}  (n={mask1.sum()}, π₁={pi1:.2f})')\n",
    "print(f'Subgroup 0: τ₀ = {tau0:.4f}  (n={mask0.sum()}, π₀={pi0:.2f})')\n",
    "print(f'Weighted:   π₁τ₁ + π₀τ₀ = {ace_check:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'Direct ACE:               = {true_ace:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'Match: {np.isclose(ace_check, true_ace)}')\n",
    "print(f'\\nBoth τ₁, τ₀ > 0? {tau1 > 0 and tau0 > 0}')\n",
    "print(f'Overall τ > 0? {true_ace > 0}')\n",
    "print('=> Yule-Simpson paradox confirmed impossible for TRUE causal effects.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Nonlinear Estimands: Median Treatment Effects\n",
    "\n",
    "Problem 2.2: Comparing δ₁ = median(Y(1)) − median(Y(0)) vs δ₂ = median(Y(1) − Y(0))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "delta1 = np.median(Y1) - np.median(Y0)\n",
    "delta2 = np.median(Y1 - Y0)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'δ₁ = median(Y(1)) − median(Y(0)) = {delta1:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'δ₂ = median(Y(1) − Y(0))         = {delta2:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'Difference δ₁ − δ₂ = {delta1 - delta2:.4f}')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('When effects are heterogeneous (as here), δ₁ ≠ δ₂.')\n",
    "print('δ₂ captures the typical individual experience;')\n",
    "print('δ₁ captures differences at the population-distribution level.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Homework Problem 2.1 Solution: Perfect Doctor Analytical Calculation\n",
    "\n",
    "Using truncated normal theory to compute E[Y|Z=1] − E[Y|Z=0]\n",
    "when Z = 1(τ ≥ 0), τ = −0.5 + Y(0), Y(0) ~ N(0,1)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from scipy.stats import norm, truncnorm\n",
    "\n",
    "# Z = 1 iff tau >= 0 iff (-0.5 + Y0) >= 0 iff Y0 >= 0.5\n",
    "# So treatment group: Y0 ~ N(0,1) truncated to [0.5, inf)\n",
    "# Control group: Y0 ~ N(0,1) truncated to (-inf, 0.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "# E[Y0 | Y0 >= 0.5] using truncated normal formula\n",
    "mu, sigma = 0, 1\n",
    "a_treat, b_treat = 0.5, np.inf\n",
    "alpha_treat = (a_treat - mu) / sigma  # = 0.5\n",
    "\n",
    "E_Y0_given_treated = mu + sigma * norm.pdf(alpha_treat) / (1 - norm.cdf(alpha_treat))\n",
    "E_tau_given_treated = -0.5 + E_Y0_given_treated\n",
    "E_Y1_given_treated = E_Y0_given_treated + E_tau_given_treated\n",
    "E_Y_given_treated = E_Y1_given_treated  # treated observe Y(1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# E[Y0 | Y0 < 0.5]\n",
    "alpha_ctrl = (0.5 - mu) / sigma  # = 0.5\n",
    "E_Y0_given_control = mu - sigma * norm.pdf(alpha_ctrl) / norm.cdf(alpha_ctrl)\n",
    "E_tau_given_control = -0.5 + E_Y0_given_control\n",
    "E_Y_given_control = E_Y0_given_control  # controls observe Y(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "analytical_dim = E_Y_given_treated - E_Y_given_control\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=== Analytical Solution for Perfect Doctor ===')\n",
    f"print(f'E[Y(0) | treated]       = {E_Y0_given_treated:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'E[Y(1) | treated]       = {E_Y1_given_treated:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'E[Y  | treated]         = {E_Y_given_treated:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'E[Y(0) | control]       = {E_Y0_given_control:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'E[Y  | control]         = {E_Y_given_control:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'E[Y|Z=1] − E[Y|Z=0]    = {analytical_dim:.4f}')\n",
    f"print(f'Simulation DiM          = {did_perfect:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'True ACE                = {-0.5 + np.mean(Y0):.4f} ≈ -0.5')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Conclusion: The perfect doctor REVERSES the sign of the effect!')\n",
    "print('True ACE ≈ -0.5, but naive DiM under perfect-doctor assignment ≈ +2.17')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Experimental Unit Subtlety Demonstration\n",
    "\n",
    "Showing why 'before/after' self-experimentation fails: it creates\n",
    "four potential outcomes (two observed, two missing), NOT two."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Simulate a self-experiment scenario\n",
    "# Person takes aspirin 'after' but not 'before'\n",
    "# Yi_before(0) = 0 (observed: headache persisted, no aspirin)\n",
    "# Yi_after(1) = 1  (observed: headache gone, took aspirin)\n",
    "# Yi_before(1) = ? (MISSING)\n",
    "# Yi_after(0)  = ? (MISSING)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=== Self-Experiment: Aspirin & Headache ===')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('| Time   | Y(0)        | Y(1)        | Observed Y |')\n",
    "print('|--------|-------------|-------------|------------|')\n",
    "print('| Before | 0 ✓ (obs)   | ? ✗ (miss)  | 0          |')\n",
    "print('| After  | ? ✗ (miss)  | 1 ✓ (obs)   | 1          |')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Individual causal effect (before): Y_before(1) - Y_before(0) = ? - 0 = UNKNOWN')\n",
    "print('Individual causal effect (after):  Y_after(1) - Y_after(0)  = 1 - ? = UNKNOWN')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Scenario A: Y_after(0) = 1 → headache would resolve anyway → τ = 0')\n",
    "print('Scenario B: Y_after(0) = 0 → aspirin caused resolution → τ = 1')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Without additional assumptions (e.g., stability of Y(0) over time),')\n",
    "print('we CANNOT determine the causal effect from self-experimentation alone.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Monte Carlo: Distribution of DiM Under Random vs. Confounded Assignment"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "n_sims = 10000\n",
    "dim_random_list = []\n",
    "dim_perfect_list = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for _ in range(n_sims):\n",
    "    Y0_sim = np.random.normal(0, 1, n)\n",
    "    tau_sim = -0.5 + Y0_sim\n",
    "    Y1_sim = Y0_sim + tau_sim\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Random assignment\n",
    "    Z_r = np.random.binomial(1, 0.5, n)\n",
    "    Y_r = Z_r * Y1_sim + (1 - Z_r) * Y0_sim\n",
    "    dim_random_list.append(Y_r[Z_r==1].mean() - Y_r[Z_r==0].mean())\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Perfect doctor\n",
    "    Z_p = (tau_sim >= 0).astype(int)\n",
    "    Y_p = Z_p * Y1_sim + (1 - Z_p) * Y0_sim\n",
    "    dim_perfect_list.append(Y_p[Z_p==1].mean() - Y_p[Z_p==0].mean())\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "ax.hist(dim_random_list, bins=50, alpha=0.6, color='#6d4aff', label=f'Random (mean={np.mean(dim_random_list):.2f})')\n",
    "ax.hist(dim_perfect_list, bins=50, alpha=0.6, color='#ff4a6d', label=f'Perfect Doctor (mean={np.mean(dim_perfect_list):.2f})')\n",
    "ax.axvline(-0.5, color='black', linewidth=2, linestyle='--', label='True ACE = −0.5')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Difference in Means (DiM)')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Frequency')\n",
    "ax.set_title(f'Monte Carlo: {n_sims} simulations — Assignment Mechanism Matters', fontsize=13)\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "| Concept | Key Insight |\n",
    "|---------|------------|\n",
    "| Science Table | The n×2 matrix of all potential outcomes — half is always missing |\n",
    "| SUTVA | No interference + consistency required for valid inference |\n",
    "| Assignment Mechanism | Determines whether naive DiM recovers the true ACE |\n",
    "| Subgroup Effects | If all subgroups positive → overall must be positive (no Simpson's paradox for true effects) |\n",
    "| Experimental Unit | Person-time, not person — self-experiments don't reveal both POs |\n",
    "| Nonlinear Estimands | δ₁ ≠ δ₂ in general; choice depends on the research question |"
   ]
  }
